---
layout: bare.njk
---
<style>
  .archive-file[data-state="fetched"] a { color: var(--bare-muted); }
  .archive-file[data-state="failed"]::after { content: " · not fetched"; color: #d9534f; }
  .archive-files { columns: 22rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; font-size: 0.85rem; }
</style>

<h1>Archive copy: {{ survey.title }}</h1>
<p>Save this page to a web archive after saving <a href="{{ ('/surveys/' + survey.id + '/') | url }}">the survey page</a>. The survey page loads its 3D playback a minute at a time, so a save of that page keeps only the start of the recording. Opening this page fetches every file the playback uses, so a save keeps them all.</p>
<p id="archive-status" role="status">Fetching the files…</p>
<noscript><p>Fetching the files needs JavaScript. They are all linked below.</p></noscript>

{% for rec in survey.recordings %}{% if rec.hasPlayback %}
<h2>{{ rec.label }}</h2>
<ul class="archive-files">
  {% for file in rec.files %}<li class="archive-file"><a href="{{ file | url }}">{{ file | replace(rec.assetsUrl + "/", "") }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}

<script type="module">
  import { mountArchivePage } from "{{ (modulesBase + '/js/survey-archive.js') | url }}";
  mountArchivePage(document);
</script>
